{
  "headline": "Ampicillin sodium is not on FDA's shortage list as of 2026-10-21; supply traces to a plant with an OAI classification in 2015 and a VAI in 2019",
  "headline_cites": ["D8", "E9", "E10"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's drug shortage list shows ampicillin sodium is not listed as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The label for NDC 83270031110 identifies the manufacturing plant as ONESOURCE SPECIALTY PHARMA LIMITED - Beta Lactam Division (FEI 3005652193) in India.",
      "cites": ["E11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 940034 at that FEI ended 2015-09-01 and was classified OAI, with the classification known to FDA on 2015-11-30.",
      "cites": ["E9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A later inspection 1079813 ended 2019-02-14 and was classified VAI, known to FDA on 2019-05-15.",
      "cites": ["E10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Sandoz Inc. has a discontinuation posting for a private‑label ampicillin sodium injection dated 2025-12-08, but this does not place the drug on the overall shortage list.",
      "cites": ["E13"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Current on‑hand inventory across Corvale East and Corvale General ranges from 12.6 to 27.6 days of supply depending on presentation and site.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2", "D3", "D4", "D5", "D6", "D7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule‑based alternate manufacturer ranked highest is Armas Pharmaceuticals Inc., which is not on the FDA shortage list today, though its label names no plant we could place.",
      "cites": ["D9"]
    }
  ]
}
